":"b269a308088a8956e31f211743ccdc381edf868b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/git/trees/b269a308088a8956e31f211743ccdc381edf868b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/git/commits/855978d03540338186e36f34d96880462e9b54c1","verification":{"payload":"tree b269a308088a8956e31f211743ccdc381edf868b\nparent fdc8af8418ec08856bef620e3cca963992e3ee8f\nparent 2d4d248dd38909dabd2fbb644c29d1b0a783ff71\nauthor Ludea <ludovicw35@hotmail.com> 1786996361 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786996361 +0200\n\nMerge pull request #1061 from gloubix/fix/stream-survives-plugin-errors\n\nfix(rpc): report plugin errors to the UI instead of ending the stream","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg2aJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFT8QAK/ITF/5crE3q/83kMJzSV7X\ngvwP81E5Gdu5y8lRLnwweGdSmr6/Hif25H7OgFjP8rJGciRH+FmIki2UbJNjUk2R\nu30A4IOxMkUmTEa4MWHrTbGIwd10rbHOyjMceGBdVAJ2Ox2WJQV8PAlpcgtnOfN8\npf1t/QcCtIsWVMmZZiJocI3DTuUx/iPgP7kMk2QoUWsf3IdhpPksKLOea9IBK4Jk\n+xMs2a+p0T9fAohIUhet8WK1SXW0GtX6eQzAc9XKhocey5kSoOCMBNfsI+Ims1ig\ndq9XozCPNZdUPIGfKMQ+6SYe+AQl56CmwCdN7jcX7LrdlWJsrYRSU1NwrBkBdXMj\nQyMZXU5FLuXWvr9OQD4P1jDEEdySjKxxSF6oEBOdhceRj2eqKut63G8zisOgUGvs\ncKEeqmB5j2/2tePONnKNeKMO8DfwT8YN+ra7QnLpF+A17KOim1AWz9bVC9ufcWNR\nl4xNvZyimCYf2qb4NMBrL5W5MlyJ62zqC+fyEtmLvLfhRSV/oEM6MZgDtWOejIQQ\nS0z1LuuR8EcNVPXu6WqAQyzacMtEXZD8PEbLVwnhk6CWNrfbR6JiZpU4vMgZ0IsA\nW0jpEP5/SzNjQsCZLCgSPr48R4KhquH+4WKtIPZ+8MaUU8IUwFcUdfZ0mdIX+KaJ\nphOX46lQ2T1d7s43pYqr\n=tAkB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-17T19:52:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ludea/Sparus/commit/855978d03540338186e36f34d96880462e9b54c1","node_id":"C_kwDOIfV2TdoAKDg1NTk3OGQwMzU0MDMzODE4NmUzNmYzNGQ5Njg4MDQ2MmU5YjU0YzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ludea/Sparus/commit/fdc8af8418ec08856bef620e3cca963992e3ee8f","sha":"fdc8af8418ec08856bef620e3cca963992e3ee8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/commits/fdc8af8418ec08856bef620e3cca963992e3ee8f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ludea/Sparus/commit/2d4d248dd38909dabd2fbb644c29d1b0a783ff71","sha":"2d4d248dd38909dabd2fbb644c29d1b0a783ff71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/commits/2d4d248dd38909dabd2fbb644c29d1b0a783ff71"}],"sha":"855978d03540338186e36f34d96880462e9b54c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/commits/855978d03540338186e36f34d96880462e9b54c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1148460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gloubix","id":1148460,"login":"gloubix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDg0NjA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/commits/2d4d248dd38909dabd2fbb644c29d1b0a783ff71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T12:03:04Z","email":"fab@igbx.fr","name":"fab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T12:03:04Z","email":"fab@igbx.fr","name":"fab"},"message":"fix(rpc): report plugin errors to the UI instead of ending the stream\n\nFixes #1060 (\"Stream closed after first event received\").\n\n## Why the stream closes\n\n`start_streaming` returns `Err(SparusError::PluginEvent(..))` when handling\nan event fails, and `start_rpc_client` then treats that as terminal:\n\n```rust\nif let Err(SparusError::PluginEvent(err)) = result {\n  return Err(SparusError::PluginEvent(format!(\n    \"Plugin event failed, stopping subscription: {err}\"\n  )));\n}\n```\n\nSo the first event whose handler fails ends the loop *and* the retry loop.\nThe launcher unsubscribes for the rest of the session and the second event\nnever arrives -- exactly the reported symptom.\n\nFailing on the first event is easy to hit: `download_and_write_file` fetches\nboth `{plugins_url}/plugins/{name}` and `{url}/frontend.js`, so a plugin\nwithout a `frontend.js` 404s; and DELETE on a plugin directory that isn''t\nthere is a `NotFound`.\n\nConnect failures were terminal too (`Err(err) => return Err(...)`), so the\nbackoff loop could only ever retry a dropped stream, never an unreachable\nCMS.\n\n## Why it went back to being terminal\n\nThat''s my fault for how I left it in #1058: I used `eprintln!`, you replaced\nit with returned errors in 040586e, which is the right instinct -- printing\nwas never going to reach anyone, and it''s the same point you made in #1017.\n\nBut returning doesn''t reach anyone either: `lib.rs:115` spawns this task and\ndrops the `JoinHandle`, so nothing ever inspects the `Result`. Returning an\nerror there only has one observable effect -- it kills the subscription.\n\n## What this does instead\n\nEmits the `SparusError` to the frontend on `sparus://pluginerror`, the same\nway `updater.rs` reports progress on `sparus://downloadinfos`, and `Footer.tsx`\nlistens for it and feeds it into `setGlobalError`. So the error is typed\n(no printing), it''s actually visible to the user, and it doesn''t take the\nsubscription down with it.\n\n`SparusError` can''t be `Clone` (it wraps `io::Error`), and `Emitter::emit`\nrequires `Serialize + Clone`, so `report` goes through `serde_json::to_value`\n-- which reuses the existing `Serialize` impl, keeping `kind` consistent with\nevery other error the UI receives.\n\n`start_rpc_client` no longer returns a `Result`: it retries connect failures\nwith the same backoff instead of giving up, and resets the backoff once a\nconnection succeeds.\n\nVerified: `cargo check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`,\n`cargo fmt --check` and `tsc --noEmit` all clean.","tree":{"sha":"b269a308088a8956e31f211743ccdc381edf868b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/git/trees/b269a308088a8956e31f211743ccdc381edf868b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/git/commits/2d4d248dd38909dabd2fbb644c29d1b0a783ff71","verification":{"payload":"tree b269a308088a8956e31f211743ccdc381edf868b\nparent fdc8af8418ec08856bef620e3cca963992e3ee8f\nauthor fab <fab@igbx.fr> 1786968184 +0200\ncommitter fab <fab@igbx.fr> 1786968184 +0200\n\nfix(rpc): report plugin errors to the UI instead of ending the stream\n\nFixes #1060 (\"Stream closed after first event received\").\n\n## Why the stream closes\n\n`start_streaming` returns `Err(SparusError::PluginEvent(..))` when handling\nan event fails, and `start_rpc_client` then treats that as terminal:\n\n```rust\nif let Err(SparusError::PluginEvent(err)) = result {\n  return Err(SparusError::PluginEvent(format!(\n    \"Plugin event failed, stopping subscription: {err}\"\n  )));\n}\n```\n\nSo the first event whose handler fails ends the loop *and* the retry loop.\nThe launcher unsubscribes for the rest of the session and the second event\nnever arrives -- exactly the reported symptom.\n\nFailing on the first event is easy to hit: `download_and_write_file` fetches\nboth `{plugins_url}/plugins/{name}` and `{url}/frontend.js`, so a plugin\nwithout a `frontend.js` 404s; and DELETE on a plugin directory that isn''t\nthere is a `NotFound`.\n\nConnect failures were terminal too (`Err(err) => return Err(...)`), so the\nbackoff loop could only ever retry a dropped stream, never an unreachable\nCMS.\n\n## Why it went back to being terminal\n\nThat''s my fault for how I left it in #1058: I used `eprintln!`, you replaced\nit with returned errors in 040586e, which is the right instinct -- printing\nwas never going to reach anyone, and it''s the same point you made in #1017.\n\nBut returning doesn''t reach anyone either: `lib.rs:115` spawns this task and\ndrops the `JoinHandle`, so nothing ever inspects the `Result`. Returning an\nerror there only has one observable effect -- it kills the subscription.\n\n## What this does instead\n\nEmits the `SparusError` to the frontend on `sparus://pluginerror`, the same\nway `updater.rs` reports progress on `sparus://downloadinfos`, and `Footer.tsx`\nlistens for it and feeds it into `setGlobalError`. So the error is typed\n(no printing), it''s actually visible to the user, and it doesn''t take the\nsubscription down with it.\n\n`SparusError` can''t be `Clone` (it wraps `io::Error`), and `Emitter::emit`\nrequires `Serialize + Clone`, so `report` goes through `serde_json::to_value`\n-- which reuses the existing `Serialize` impl, keeping `kind` consistent with\nevery other error the UI receives.\n\n`start_rpc_client` no longer returns a `Result`: it retries connect failures\nwith the same backoff instead of giving up, and resets the backoff once a\nconnection succeeds.\n\nVerified: `cargo check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`,\n`cargo fmt --check` and `tsc --noEmit` all clean.\n","reason":"bad_email","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCAAdFiEEZ1Y6THXvniR7EA96YBank9INgXgFAmqC+HgACgkQYBank9IN\ngXh71RAAsvtRhZwhVycWYHOjgbylw+YjMnKJ8Psk4fPZ7ym2vs2mrnzNMzF47xvi\nbE97tiefIH0mnbLLKqiSSNJShWdzr1ox9ClTSQaIiProtJ0cJctyzXXRPxYHNN3u\nIbxWrZeQh9KvEdDG2QNSONiu1jmM3zlRNYNNH3B+fIDR8GDvWjflFjIunPizy89f\ntCR2yr9h3M4awXjzt2F1iAglVI7vjhMhox70FywNTqytyq1iEm/GVokyA5y03q7Q\nCL7yRjSeqiY9pXLi1NpVXUnpuxK9M1G4+XtN80WXiBXRE2lS2eZqX/cwzfAg9XP0\ntQlReTFGHtarHMsF7GYhWW623MDM/29Vzf2Haxr1VqucJdiuy5VXrgz6FwwLzDj9\nERNOCfg0H1mICx/d/gtv0EzE+jv9d8oqklt9zO8fsNHagUzj9Wuna66aT74vg42m\nUNxeLpQYxLPr6VEYnYj1dR7RMDgnZPZaoFvWNkVSAMp+Zx1vGy8gCNa/rW14LgsF\naFRkALneB1jlSkpNPPHU0m9vkEedUH2jezNS4gZ+14sYUu8u2rOW/BDKtMgy/G1M\nY94tB57FdX1frsUut0jOznhZVOTqa0zu6rwBeZqwvL7ePSmQvOBeqcTDBICQMMEt\nmci5N8ocxdA/9CB2jcWwcaYuNDVA/LXyx75pv114UB0YR+cFsOE=\n=oRVl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1148460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gloubix","id":1148460,"login":"gloubix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDg0NjA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://a