rganizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ludea/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ludea/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ludea/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ludea/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ludea/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ludea","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ludea/Sparus/commit/6d47ee515af7900bc681bab8ed31bb79b62c17c1","node_id":"C_kwDOIfV2TdoAKDZkNDdlZTUxNWFmNzkwMGJjNjgxYmFiOGVkMzFiYjc5YjYyYzE3YzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ludea/Sparus/commit/89c51e8afcbf068c1ade2ee07ee971dbe970c973","sha":"89c51e8afcbf068c1ade2ee07ee971dbe970c973","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/commits/89c51e8afcbf068c1ade2ee07ee971dbe970c973"}],"sha":"6d47ee515af7900bc681bab8ed31bb79b62c17c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/commits/6d47ee515af7900bc681bab8ed31bb79b62c17c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1148460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gloubix","id":1148460,"login":"gloubix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDg0NjA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/commits/c90a0465bfa75997d4328711534b1f0893afabc7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T13:04:14Z","email":"francois.baldi@igbx.fr","name":"gloubix"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T13:04:14Z","email":"francois.baldi@igbx.fr","name":"gloubix"},"message":"fix(rpc): survive stream errors instead of unsubscribing silently\n\nCompanion to the Lucle-side fix for \"send_event_all reaches no client\"\n(Ludea/lucle). The server bug is fixed there; this is the client half,\nwhich turns any single failure into permanent silence.\n\n## What was wrong\n\n`while let Ok(Some(item)) = stream.message().await` matched only\n`Ok(Some(..))`. `Streaming::message()` has three outcomes, and the other\ntwo both exited the loop:\n\n- `Ok(None)`  -> clean end of stream\n- `Err(status)` -> the server pushed a Status, or the transport failed\n\nThe `Err` case didn''t even bind the status: it was dropped by the failed\npattern match, `start_streaming` returned `Ok(())`, and the launcher went\npermanently silent while looking perfectly healthy. There is no logging\nin this crate, so nothing was visible anywhere.\n\nInside the loop, `download_and_write_file(..).await?` and\n`remove_dir_all(..).await?` propagated out of the loop too — so a single\n404 on one plugin (or an already-deleted directory) ended the whole\nsubscription, not just that one event. That''s the \"it worked once and\nthen stopped\" shape.\n\nFinally `start_rpc_client` connected exactly once. `EventClient::connect`\nis eager, so if the CMS wasn''t up yet when the launcher started — the\nnormal case for a desktop launcher — the task ended immediately and never\nretried. Its `JoinHandle` is dropped at the `tauri::async_runtime::spawn`\ncall site, so the `Result` was discarded either way.\n\n## What this changes\n\n- Match the three `message()` outcomes explicitly; a stream error is now\n  returned rather than silently swallowed.\n- A failed install/update/delete for one plugin is logged and skipped;\n  the subscription keeps running.\n- An unknown event type is logged instead of ending the stream. It''s\n  still built as `SparusError::PluginEvent` (per the #1017 review), just\n  reported rather than returned — a build that doesn''t recognise an event\n  shouldn''t unsubscribe from all future ones. It also now names the\n  actual numeric type: the old code re-ran the `try_from` that had just\n  failed, so the message was always literally \"UNKNOWN_EVENT\".\n- `start_rpc_client` reconnects with exponential backoff (1s, doubling,\n  capped at 60s), resetting after a successful connect. It no longer\n  returns a `Result` since nothing could observe it.\n\nErrors go to `eprintln!` because this crate has no logging framework and\nadding one is your call — happy to wire up `tauri-plugin-log` instead if\nyou''d prefer. Note release builds set `windows_subsystem = \"windows\"`, so\non Windows these are only visible in a dev build.\n\nVerified: `cargo check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`\nclean, `cargo fmt --check` clean.","tree":{"sha":"db4b778b53b03bb8ba1f3ef02c2c65b1846d91a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/git/trees/db4b778b53b03bb8ba1f3ef02c2c65b1846d91a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ludea/Sparus/git/commits/c90a0465bfa75997d4328711534b1f0893afabc7","verification":{"payload":"tree db4b778b53b03bb8ba1f3ef02c2c65b1846d91a0\nparent 89c51e8afcbf068c1ade2ee07ee971dbe970c973\nauthor gloubix <francois.baldi@igbx.fr> 1786539854 +0200\ncommitter gloubix <francois.baldi@igbx.fr> 1786539854 +0200\n\nfix(rpc): survive stream errors instead of unsubscribing silently\n\nCompanion to the Lucle-side fix for \"send_event_all reaches no client\"\n(Ludea/lucle). The server bug is fixed there; this is the client half,\nwhich turns any single failure into permanent silence.\n\n## What was wrong\n\n`while let Ok(Some(item)) = stream.message().await` matched only\n`Ok(Some(..))`. `Streaming::message()` has three outcomes, and the other\ntwo both exited the loop:\n\n- `Ok(None)`  -> clean end of stream\n- `Err(status)` -> the server pushed a Status, or the transport failed\n\nThe `Err` case didn''t even bind the status: it was dropped by the failed\npattern match, `start_streaming` returned `Ok(())`, and the launcher went\npermanently silent while looking perfectly healthy. There is no logging\nin this crate, so nothing was visible anywhere.\n\nInside the loop, `download_and_write_file(..).await?` and\n`remove_dir_all(..).await?` propagated out of the loop too — so a single\n404 on one plugin (or an already-deleted directory) ended the whole\nsubscription, not just that one event. That''s the \"it worked once and\nthen stopped\" shape.\n\nFinally `start_rpc_client` connected exactly once. `EventClient::connect`\nis eager, so if the CMS wasn''t up yet when the launcher started — the\nnormal case for a desktop launcher — the task ended immediately and never\nretried. Its `JoinHandle` is dropped at the `tauri::async_runtime::spawn`\ncall site, so the `Result` was discarded either way.\n\n## What this changes\n\n- Match the three `message()` outcomes explicitly; a stream error is now\n  returned rather than silently swallowed.\n- A failed install/update/delete for one plugin is logged and skipped;\n  the subscription keeps running.\n- An unknown event type is logged instead of ending the stream. It''s\n  still built as `SparusError::PluginEvent` (per the #1017 review), just\n  reported rather than returned — a build that doesn''t recognise an event\n  shouldn''t unsubscribe from all future ones. It also now names the\n  actual numeric type: the old code re-ran the `try_from` that had just\n  failed, so the message was always literally \"UNKNOWN_EVENT\".\n- `start_rpc_client` reconnects with exponential backoff (1s, doubling,\n  capped at 60s), resetting after a successful connect. It no longer\n  returns a `Result` since nothing could observe it.\n\nErrors go to `eprintln!` because this crate has no logging framework and\nadding one is your call — happy to wire up `tauri-plugin-log` instead if\nyou''d prefer. Note release builds set `windows_subsystem = \"windows\"`, so\non Windows these are only visible in a dev build.\n\nVerified: `cargo check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`\nclean, `cargo fmt --check` clean.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCAAdFiEEZ1Y6THXvniR7EA96YBank9INgXgFAmp8b04ACgkQYBank9IN\ngXidhw//X988rIsHzi+5NvyOMy17BgWbyfVljd6tQMyILzVLFxRdAj+DGP2I8GQ4\nTFdzmcOfFXrcTyv2cirjlINzhgIwz89KhJu3bx63kCo+yDI8ulLTYLKfBUijh3CR\nHD94oR403HMTT1mcSj8CGBujYVEh9Fhzs5mkUDyQpzJOwi6z6UNn0FgiSwHxNrIT\nMeBuwIW3eFT05PK3SVBTjT/32r0eXwbOJo4QIKRS7K/zC96xX+SP7wMbWhHz8tFd\n3MWhfkyAL2dZGIFtICu2YYEL/Ngv1m2C7nORfp6dJEwUVF7KiF8M73em5kh9KKpz\nIfQpi0afQw2J0rDCLncovW1/A+idsz5sasU6ktoHeWmCwpnWY0KiMpjp+QxTWa1Z\ndZNEtMBhea1ZOWokKAwYUgdHVuBxY6OJl4lhXQReBstomtXLWJB0rItBfmFMRgo1\nBjcn9pRJzX+KKUiMQle4mcNVtGIVrsLpZR+uST2hRd09a9ZvJKGboBY9W0u95OnH\ngIcrRT++FdUaOs9rIRqifZOaibeiXPu2wXU244Mqdk8AHwU7qsk+2Csdyi3vDu68\nfYmqhNZUbITuoZFEVnucwlFXUXyj0bncuqAtirWY3IQE60j+gblYf0s+IlW/xSrq\nYNgzOgUtTq+asIeHF/2j+7HqFsZ7J5kXC5iqcU573/GlfWMZwsU=\n=CGxi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T16:48:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1148460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gloubix","id":1148460,"login":"gloubix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDg0NjA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gloubix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/u