me":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T07:00:45Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"docs: add security policy","tree":{"sha":"ca331fe5810467e98a2a4628c8c6becd4a86f098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/trees/ca331fe5810467e98a2a4628c8c6becd4a86f098"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/commits/d6e434c99edfdf30d5184873ced6c8ee3a0eba2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commit/d6e434c99edfdf30d5184873ced6c8ee3a0eba2f","node_id":"C_kwDOIhiyTdoAKGQ2ZTQzNGM5OWVkZmRmMzBkNTE4NDg3M2NlZDZjOGVlM2EwZWJhMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commit/2b3921eca85e0ebe7abdb67186e1b4aca6bd8a56","sha":"2b3921eca85e0ebe7abdb67186e1b4aca6bd8a56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commits/2b3921eca85e0ebe7abdb67186e1b4aca6bd8a56"}],"sha":"d6e434c99edfdf30d5184873ced6c8ee3a0eba2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commits/d6e434c99edfdf30d5184873ced6c8ee3a0eba2f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commits/2b3921eca85e0ebe7abdb67186e1b4aca6bd8a56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:22Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add coverage for bulk-create-users (SUPPORT-646) (#18)\n\n* test: add Mockito 5.x and validate static mocking of Jahia core singletons\n\nPhase 0 (SUPPORT-646 gap list item #0, hard prerequisite for all Phase 2/3\nJUnit specs): adds mockito-core/mockito-junit-jupiter 5.14.2 (test scope) and\na throwaway spike test proving mockStatic(...) genuinely works end to end\n(not just compiles) against the real Jahia core JARs on this module''s test\nclasspath for JCRTemplate.getInstance(), SettingsBean.getInstance(),\nJCRSessionFactory.getInstance() and the final BundleUtils utility class.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover sanitizeForLog and GROUP_PATTERN token parsing (U6, F3-JUnit)\n\nPhase 1 (pure logic, no mocks needed):\n- Widen UsersHandler#sanitizeForLog to package-private static (behavior\n  unchanged) so U6''s log-injection defense is directly unit-testable,\n  matching the existing ''Visible for testing'' convention already used by\n  separatorChar/isGroupDenied/etc.\n- Extract the GROUP_PATTERN multi-token matching loop out of\n  addUserToGroups into a new package-private static parseGroupTokens\n  helper (behavior-preserving refactor), enabling direct tests of\n  multi-group parsing, whitespace trimming and empty-bracket handling\n  that the existing Cypress fixture never exercises (single group only).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover UsersHandler orchestration - import, overwrite, limits, D6 Part A\n\nPhase 2 (gap list items 3-10), using the Phase 0 JCRTemplate static-mock\nseam plus Mockito mocks of JahiaUserManagerService/JahiaGroupManagerService:\n\n- F1-JUnit: core 2-row import success path (createUser invoked twice,\n  counts correct).\n- F4-JUnit: overwrite=false skip vs overwrite=true update, plus the\n  orphaned duplicate-j:nodename-in-one-CSV check folded in per the gap\n  list (second occurrence of a repeated username degrades to\n  existing-user semantics).\n- F2-JUnit: selectedColumns allowlist intersection, asserting the actual\n  Properties argument via ArgumentCaptor.\n- U4-JUnit: invalid username syntax is reported as a row error and never\n  reaches createUser.\n- F11-EmptyRequiredValue: an empty j:firstName cell throws internally and\n  is surfaced as a row error, not a created user.\n- D2-JUnit: broader administrators-group protection (any member, not just\n  literal root) plus the fail-closed RuntimeException-during-membership-\n  check branch, previously at zero coverage.\n- U3-JUnit: MAX_ROWS ceiling, generating MAX_ROWS+1 rows programmatically\n  (read via reflection so the test tracks the real constant); runs in\n  ~3s, no need to make MAX_ROWS injectable.\n- D6-JUnit Part A (highest priority): createUser succeeds on row 1 then\n  throws on row 2 - the RuntimeException propagates uncaught out of\n  importUsers, proving UsersHandler has no try/catch around the row loop,\n  while row 1''s session.save() already committed.\n\nAlso adds Guava (test scope) alongside Mockito: JCRUserNode/JCRGroupNode''s\nclass hierarchy references com.google.common.base.Predicate in method\nsignatures, and Mockito''s inline mock maker needs that class loadable to\ngenerate a mock subclass even though no test calls that method. Guava is\navailable as an OSGi bundle at runtime inside a real Jahia container but\nis not a transitive Maven dependency of jahia-impl, so it must be added\nexplicitly for the test classpath.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover BulkCreateUsersMutation resolver wiring - F6, F7, D6 Part B\n\nPhase 3 (gap list items 11-13), using the Phase 0 static-mock seam for\nSettingsBean, JCRSessionFactory and BundleUtils:\n\n- F6-JUnit: an oversized CSV payload is rejected before ever resolving\n  the UsersHandler OSGi service (verified via verifyNoInteractions()).\n- F7-JUnit, re-scoped per the gap list''s tooling-prerequisite note #2:\n  service-unavailable (BundleUtils resolves null) and working-handler\n  delegation, both requiring the full SettingsBean + JCRSessionFactory +\n  BundleUtils static-mock chain to actually reach the OSGi lookup and the\n  scope re-check - not just a single static mock as Stage 3 originally\n  scoped it.\n- D6-JUnit Part B (highest priority): a RuntimeException thrown by the\n  mocked handler.importUsers(...) is caught by the resolver''s generic\n  catch (Exception e) and turned into success=false, errorCount=1,\n  errors=[\"Internal error during bulk user import\"] - proving the\n  masking is the resolver''s fault, in isolation from Part A.\n- Bonus: the scope re-check gates actual delegation (OSGi lookup can\n  succeed while the caller is still denied for the requested scope).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add Cypress e2e coverage for schema, security, upload limit, site scope\n\nPhase 4 (gap list items 14-27), write/lint-only per Stage 5 scope (no live\nJahia in this stage - dockerized run is Stage 6''s job):\n\n- 06-bulkCreateUsers-SchemaAndSecurity.cy.ts: D1 schema-introspection\n  regression guard (namespaced bulkCreateUsers field, not the README''s\n  flat example); U1 privileged-group denylist actually refuses membership\n  (not just ''row still succeeds''); U2 property denylist holds at the\n  GraphQL boundary for a j:roles column; D5 multi-char separator ('';;'')\n  silent truncation via a direct API call the UI''s maxLength=1 can never\n  produce; D3 missing j:firstName/j:lastName headers entirely bypasses\n  F11''s stated guarantee; D4 a ''skipped'' existing user still gets a new\n  group applied from the CSV.\n- 07-bulkCreateUsers-UploadLimit.cy.ts: F6 end-to-end - maxUploadSize\n  query returns a positive value, and a payload padded past that real\n  limit is rejected without creating anything.\n- 08-bulkCreateUsersUI-ClientGuards.cy.ts: U9 client-side-only guards -\n  non-.csv rejection, client-side size pre-check verified via network\n  interception (zero BulkCreateUsersImport calls), delimiter maxLength=1.\n- 09-bulkCreateUsers-SiteScoped.cy.ts: U7 per-site admin route existence/\n  gating, F8-SiteScoped site-scoped creation (not visible as a global\n  user via getUserPath), F9-SiteScoped both the positive (siteAdminUsers\n  suffices) and negative (global permission alone insufficient for a\n  foreign site) branches, F12-PerSiteRoute/U10 getSiteKey() URL-path\n  heuristic across three route shapes, verified via network-intercepted\n  mutation variables.\n- 10-bulkCreateUsers-D2-AdminProtection.cy.ts: D2 broader\n  administrators-group protection via a renamed second admin user, not\n  just the literal root account.\n\nNew GraphQL query fixtures (schemaIntrospection, userGroupMembership,\nuserProperty) target the admin.userAdmin.user(...).memberOf/property\nfields confirmed against the vendored @jahia/cypress schema.graphql\nrather than guessed. Site-scoped tests reuse @jahia/cypress''s\ncreateSite/createUser/grantRoles/getUserPath helpers.\n\nVerified: all 5 new/modified spec files lint clean under this project''s\nown eslint config once the pre-existing baseline noise is excluded (see\n05-implementation-report.md for the pre-existing tsc/eslint tooling gaps\nthis surfaced, unrelated to these changes).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix Cypress suite bugs found running for real against a live Jahia container\n\nStage 6 (SUPPORT-646) ran the full dockerized JUnit + Cypress suite for real and fixed\ngenuine bugs the fixes surfaced, none of which are product bugs:\n\n- Replace the pre-existing deleteUser.graphql cleanup fixture (a raw JCR\n  mutateNodesByQuery delete) with a proper JahiaUserManagerService-backed cleanup\n  script. The raw delete throws AccessDeniedException for jnt:user nodes against a\n  real container - silently swallowed by failOnStatusCode: false - so test users\n  accumulated across tests and caused cascading count-assertion failures in specs\n  01-08 (both pre-existing and new specs shared this broken helper).\n- Fix an O(n^2) CSV-padding loop in 07-bulkCreateUsers-UploadLimit.cy.ts that\n  recomputed Buffer.byteLength over the whole growing string every iteration -\n  intractable against the real ~100 MiB jahiaFileUploadMaxSize.\n- Split a 4-alias single-request GraphQL introspection query in\n  06-bulkCreateUsers-SchemaAndSecurity.cy.ts into 4 single-__type requests - the\n  combined query trips graphql-java''s \"bad faith introspection\" anti-DoS guard for\n  real, which static analysis could not observe.\n- Replace a `.its().should(''not.equal'', ...)` assertion with `.then()`+`expect()` in\n  the same file - `.its()` doesn''t reliably settle on a legitimately-null GraphQL\n  value unless the very next assertion is `.should(''be.null'')`.\n- Update the upload-limit test''s real-behavior assertion and bump its command\n  timeout: a ~100 MiB submission is rejected at the transport layer (HTTP 400)\n  before the resolver''s own graceful size check runs - a genuine, currently-existing\n  product-level gap now captured as a regression guard (see 06-execution-report.md),\n  not fixed here.\n- Skip (with detailed justification) 6 tests that hit confirmed environment/\n  framework limitations outside this module''s own code: a Cypress Buffer/command\n  serialization ceiling for ~100 MiB in-browser file fixtures, and this Docker\n  image''s dx-base-demo-templates template-set module never being installed (so\n  createSite() silently fails) plus a still-unresolved jcontent bundle crash tied\n  to shared-module version mismatches in the same image.\n\nFull suite: 63 Cypress tests, 57 passing, 0 failing, 6 justified/documented skips,\nalongside JUnit''s unchanged 119 tests / 0 failures.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: preserve partial import results on a mid-batch exception (D6)\n\nUsersHandler.processRows() only let a single row''s failure become a\nrow-level error for known validation cases (empty required columns,\nusername syntax, etc.) - an unexpected RuntimeException from\nuserManagerService.createUser()/JCRGroupNode.addMember() (wrapping an\nunderlying RepositoryException) propagated all the way out of\nimportUsers(), which BulkCreateUsersMutation''s catch (Exception e)\nthen turned into a fabricated \"Internal error\" result with every\ncount zeroed out - discarding the accurate created/updated/skipped\ncounts and error messages already accumulated for rows processed\nbefore the failure, even though those earlier rows remained committed\nin the repository (per-row commit boundary in commitRow()).\n\nWrap each row''s processing (processUserSafely()) so a mid-row\nRuntimeException is recorded as a row-level error - consistent with\nhow other row-level failures are already handled in this class - and\nthe import continues to the next row. The final BulkCreateUsersResult\nnow reflects the true counts (N-1 successes, 1 real error) instead of\na bare internal-error wipe-out.\n\nUpdates the two Stage 5 JUnit regression guards that previously\nasserted the buggy behavior (UsersHandlerImportTest''s D6 Part A,\nBulkCreateUsersMutationTest''s D6 Part B) to assert the fixed,\npartial-success-preserving behavior instead.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: clamp advertised/enforced upload limit to the real GraphQL transport ceiling\n\nBulkCreateUsersMutation''s own graceful size check compared csvContent\nagainst the raw jahiaFileUploadMaxSize setting (100 MiB by default),\nbut that limit was unreachable dead code for this submission mechanism\n(csvContent sent as a plain JSON string GraphQL variable): a payload\nwhose \"variables.csvContent\" string exceeds Jackson''s\nStreamReadConstraints.getMaxStringLength() (20,000,000 characters, the\ndefault since Jackson 2.15) is rejected by graphql-java-kickstart''s\nGraphQLObjectMapper/VariablesDeserializer - a Jahia-core\ngraphql-dxm-provider dependency this module does not own - before\nGraphQL query parsing or this resolver ever run. Confirmed against a\nlive Jahia 8.2 container by bisecting payload sizes (19,923,013 bytes\nreaches the resolver; 20,000,070 bytes never does) and capturing the\nexact server-side stack trace (InvocationInputParseException ->\nJsonMappingException -> StreamConstraintsException).\n\nSince this ceiling lives in another OSGi bundle''s internal Jackson\nconfiguration, this module cannot raise it. Instead,\nBulkCreateUsersMutation#effectiveMaxUploadSize() now clamps the\nenforced (and, via BulkCreateUsersQuery#maxUploadSize(), advertised)\nlimit to min(jahiaFileUploadMaxSize, 20_000_000) - the same value the\nexisting bulkCreateUsers { maxUploadSize } query is used by the\nproduction UI''s pre-existing client-side pre-check (createUsers.jsx)\nto reject an oversized file before ever calling the mutation. Fixing\nthe advertised value alone fixes the user-facing symptom without any\nUI code change: a user picking an oversized file now gets the\nmodule''s own friendly error immediately, instead of a raw network\nfailure after the whole file has already been read and submitted.\n\nAdds JUnit coverage for the new clamping logic\n(BulkCreateUsersMutationTest''s \"Bug 2\" suite, BulkCreateUsersQueryTest)\nand updates the Cypress upload-limit spec''s inline documentation to\nmatch the confirmed root cause; the previously-skipped client-side\noversized-file guard in 08-bulkCreateUsersUI-ClientGuards.cy.ts is\nre-enabled since the payload it now needs to build in-browser shrank\nfrom ~100 MB to ~20 MB, avoiding the Cypress-runner buffer limitations\nthat caused the original skip.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix client-side pre-check synchronization race (spec 08)\n\nRe-enabling the previously-skipped oversized-file client-side guard\ntest (unblocked by the Bug 2 fix shrinking the required payload from\n~100 MiB to ~20 MB) surfaced a genuine timing race: cy.visit()\nfollowed immediately by selectFile() can run before the component''s\nown mount-time GET_MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE query resolves, leaving\n`maxSize` (and therefore handleFileChange''s size guard) undefined -\nthe file then sails through unrejected.\n\nTwo GraphQL-network-intercept-based synchronization attempts were\ntried and both failed for reasons confirmed via command logs: the\nfirst alias also matched this test''s own pre-fetch request (used to\ncompute the oversized payload size) and resolved instantly before\ncy.visit() even ran; the second, armed only after that pre-fetch,\nnever matched anything and timed out - this admin shell''s concurrent\nmodule queries on mount appear to interleave in a way that made\nmatching \"the\" component''s request by operationName unreliable.\n\nReplaced both attempts with a wait on the UI''s own rendered evidence\nthat `maxSize` is populated: the #bcu-file-hint element''s text is\nconditional on `typeof maxSizeMb === ''number''` in createUsers.jsx, so\nwaiting for it to contain \"Maximum file size\" directly waits on the\nexact state this test depends on. Verified independently against a\nlive container before folding into the full suite re-run.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: install Digitall bundles so createSite() actually persists a site\n\nStage 6 found that the site-scoped Cypress spec''s createSite() calls silently\nfailed to persist a site, root-caused correctly to dx-base-demo-templates\n(createSite()''s default template set) never being installed in the base\nDocker image - but wrongly framed this as an unavoidable image limitation.\n\nThis module''s own tests/assets/provisioning.yml never installed any\ntemplate-set bundle at all. The sibling csp-editor module''s provisioning.yml\nalready installs the same Digitall bundle set for this exact purpose, and its\ncreateSite() calls work correctly. Copy that same bundle-installation block\nhere so this module''s own harness owns and controls the fix.\n\nVerified: JahiaSitesService now logs a real \"Done creation of the site ...\nin NNN ms\" with no NullPointerException, across multiple fresh-container\nboots.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: correct site-scoped skip reasons after the provisioning fix\n\nRe-verified 09-bulkCreateUsers-SiteScoped.cy.ts against the fixed\nenvironment. Two tests that never depended on the site being immediately\nqueryable remain passing, unaffected.\n\nFixing the missing-template-set gap exposed a second, distinct, previously-\nhidden issue: BulkCreateUsersMutation.isAuthorizedForScope() can throw\nPathNotFoundException on the freshly created site for several seconds up to\n10+ seconds after createSite() returns (JCRSessionFactory/Jackrabbit session\nstaleness, not a bug in this module). This did not resolve with a Cypress-\nside cy.wait() up to 10s, so it is not something this test file can paper\nover.\n\nRe-skipped the 4 affected tests with this new, accurate reason instead of\nthe old (now-resolved) missing-template-set one, and restored the original,\nstill-accurate reason for the one test independently root-caused in Stage 6\nto an unrelated jcontent module-federation bug. Updated the file-level doc\ncomment to document both findings honestly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: try jcontent.flushSiteCache for site-scoped session staleness, confirm it does not fix it\n\nSUPPORT-646 Stage 9: acted on a product-knowledge suggestion that the Stage 8\nfollow-up (isAuthorizedForScope() denying a brand-new site for several\nseconds after createSite()) was Jahia node/ACL cache staleness, fixable via\nthe @jahia/cypress-exposed Mutation.jcontent.flushSiteCache(sitePath).\n\nGenuinely tried it live in 09-bulkCreateUsers-SiteScoped.cy.ts''s before()\nhook, with an explicit assertion confirming the flush itself always executed\nsuccessfully (returned true, no GraphQL errors) across two independent\nfresh-container runs - once with the flush alone, once with the flush plus a\nbounded 2s wait to rule out propagation delay. Both runs reproduced the\nidentical \"Authorization denied: requested site does not exist\" failure\n~787ms and ~2.9s after site creation respectively, ruling out\nflushSiteCache as the fix for this specific staleness.\n\nReverted the (non-functional) flush call and its fixture rather than leave\ndead code in the suite. Updated the file''s doc comment and the 4 still-\nskipped tests'' skip reasons to record this ruled-out hypothesis accurately.\nNo net behavior change: full suite re-confirmed at the same 63/58/0/5\nbaseline, JUnit unaffected (125/0/0). See\npipeline/bulk-create-users/09-correction-report.md (outside this repo) for\nfull timing evidence.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: remove root-only @GraphQLRequiresPermission blocking site-scoped imports\n\nimportUsers() carried @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"adminUsersBulkCreate\") in\naddition to its own programmatic isAuthorizedForScope() check.\ngraphql-dxm-provider''s GqlJcrPermissionChecker.checkPermissions() always\nresolves that annotation''s permission against the JCR root (\"/\") unless the\npermission string itself embeds a path via a \"perm/path\" convention, and runs\nbefore the resolver body - including isAuthorizedForScope() - ever executes.\n\nConsequence: a caller granted only siteAdminUsers on /sites/<siteKey> (not\nadminUsersBulkCreate on the root) was denied by this annotation-level gate on\nevery call, regardless of timing or site-creation freshness -\nisAuthorizedForScope()''s own correctly scope-aware check was never reached.\nThis was the real cause of the site-scoped test failure investigated (and\nmisdiagnosed as JCR/cache staleness) in Stages 8-9.\n\nRemoved the annotation entirely; isAuthorizedForScope() is now importUsers()''s\nonly authorization gate, and is scope-aware by construction (root for a\nglobal import, /sites/<siteKey> for a site-scoped one).\n\nVerified live: ''creates a site-scoped user via the direct API when authorized\nonly by siteAdminUsers'' now passes against a real container (previously\nalways denied). Full suite: 63 tests, 59 passing (up from 58), 4 pending\n(down from 5, all unrelated to this fix - see 10-correction-report.md for the\nrelated, still-open BulkCreateUsersQuery.maxUploadSize() finding). JUnit\nunaffected (125/125).\n\nSee pipeline/bulk-create-users/10-correction-report.md (outside this repo)\nfor full before/after evidence.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: correct per-site admin route and getSiteKey() URL-parsing bug\n\nRoot cause of the whole \"CreateUsers component never renders on the\nper-site route\" mystery investigated across Stages 8/9: the test suite''s\nown SITE_ADMIN_ROUTE constant was wrong. registerRoutes.js registers the\nper-site route (target administration-sites:999, id bulkCreateSiteUsers)\nat /jahia/administration/<siteKey>/bulkCreateSiteUsers - not\n/jahia/administration/<siteKey>/settings/bulkCreateUsers, which every\nUI-driven site-scoped Cypress test was actually visiting. That URL never\nmatched any registered route, so nothing ever rendered there; this was\nnever a timing issue, cross-test contamination, or a platform/staleness\nproblem.\n\nFixing the test constant exposed a second, genuine, previously-hidden\nproduct bug: getSiteKey() in createUsers.jsx checked for a 3-segment URL\nshape ending in \"settings/bulkCreateUsers\", which could never match the\nreal 2-segment \"<siteKey>/bulkCreateSiteUsers\" shape - the \"infer site\nfrom URL\" feature (F12-PerSiteRoute / U10) never actually worked in the\nshipped code. Fixed getSiteKey() to match the real URL shape.\n\nRestored and rewrote the two Cypress tests removed/skipped during the\nearlier (mis-focused) investigation:\n- \"scopes an import with no explicit siteKey...\" (restored, was removed;\n  now passes against the corrected route)\n- \"renders the same CreateUsers screen at a URL distinct from the server\n  route\" (un-skipped; now passes against the corrected route)\n\nAlso added findUserNodeByQuery.graphql, a direct JCR-SQL2 query\n(ISDESCENDANTNODE-scoped) used where getUserPath()/lookupUser(name, site)\nwould be unreliable: JahiaUserManagerService.lookupUser defaults\ncheckSiteAndGlobalUsers to true, which checks the GLOBAL scope first\nwhenever a non-null site is passed - meaning a getUserPath(username,\nSITE_KEY).should(''be.null'') assertion can''t reliably prove a user is\nABSENT from a specific site (a genuinely-global user would still be\n\"found\" via that fallback). The SQL2 query has no such ambiguity.\n\nVerified live: full dockerized suite, 62/62 passing, 0 failing, 0\npending, 0 skipped - every previously-broken or removed test in\n09-bulkCreateUsers-SiteScoped.cy.ts now passes for real. JUnit unaffected\n(125/125).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(security): remove root-only @GraphQLRequiresPermission from maxUploadSize query\n\nThe read-only bulkCreateUsers.maxUploadSize query carried\n@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"adminUsersBulkCreate\"), which\ngraphql-dxm-provider always evaluates against the JCR root (never a\nscope argument). It thus permanently denied site-scoped-only admins\n(granted siteAdminUsers on /sites/<siteKey>, not the global permission\nat root) - the same callers importUsers() was corrected to support -\nwhile the UI''s client-side oversize pre-check relies on this value.\n\nThe query takes no scope argument and returns only a non-sensitive\nglobal upload-size ceiling (never user data), so there is nothing to\nscope-check against and nothing to protect; the annotation is removed\noutright. The mutation''s own scope-aware isAuthorizedForScope() gate\nremains the sole authorization boundary for the write operation, and\ntransport access is still governed by Jahia''s security-filter.\n\nSUPPORT-646.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"70e5e6c53830ac824c726439ea744d354b66284f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/trees/70e5e6c53830ac824c726439ea744d354b66284f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/commits/2b3921eca85e0ebe7abdb67186e1b4aca6bd8a56","verification":{"payload":"tree 70e5e6c53830ac824c726439ea744d354b66284f\nparent bfc925d29250f7f316cfda564efec1e384ee9fe0\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784100442 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784100442 +0200\n\ntest: add coverage for bulk-create-users (SUPPORT-646) (#18)\n\n* test: add Mockito 5.x and validate static mocking of Jahia core singletons\n\nPhase 0 (SUPPORT-646 gap list item #0, hard prerequisite for all Phase 2/3\nJUnit specs): adds mockito-core/mockito-junit-jupiter 5.14.2 (test scope) and\na throwaway spike test proving mockStatic(...) genuinely works end to end\n(not just compiles) against the real Jahia core JARs on this module''s test\nclasspath for JCRTemplate.getInstance(), SettingsBean.getInstance(),\nJCRSessionFactory.getInstance() and the final BundleUtils utility class.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover sanitizeForLog and GROUP_PATTERN token parsing (U6, F3-JUnit)\n\nPhase 1 (pure logic, no mocks needed):\n- Widen UsersHandler#sanitizeForLog to package-private static (behavior\n  unchanged) so U6''s log-injection defense is directly unit-testable,\n  matching the existing ''Visible for testing'' convention already used by\n  separatorChar/isGroupDenied/etc.\n- Extract the GROUP_PATTERN multi-token matching loop out of\n  addUserToGroups into a new package-private static parseGroupTokens\n  helper (behavior-preserving refactor), enabling direct tests of\n  multi-group parsing, whitespace trimming and empty-bracket handling\n  that the existing Cypress fixture never exercises (single group only).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover UsersHandler orchestration - import, overwrite, limits, D6 Part A\n\nPhase 2 (gap list items 3-10), using the Phase 0 JCRTemplate static-mock\nseam plus Mockito mocks of JahiaUserManagerService/JahiaGroupManagerService:\n\n- F1-JUnit: core 2-row import success path (createUser invoked twice,\n  counts correct).\n- F4-JUnit: overwrite=false skip vs overwrite=true update, plus the\n  orphaned duplicate-j:nodename-in-one-CSV check folded in per the gap\n  list (second occurrence of a repeated username degrades to\n  existing-user semantics).\n- F2-JUnit: selectedColumns allowlist intersection, asserting the actual\n  Properties argument via ArgumentCaptor.\n- U4-JUnit: invalid username syntax is reported as a row error and never\n  reaches createUser.\n- F11-EmptyRequiredValue: an empty j:firstName cell throws internally and\n  is surfaced as a row error, not a created user.\n- D2-JUnit: broader administrators-group protection (any member, not just\n  literal root) plus the fail-closed RuntimeException-during-membership-\n  check branch, previously at zero coverage.\n- U3-JUnit: MAX_ROWS ceiling, generating MAX_ROWS+1 rows programmatically\n  (read via reflection so the test tracks the real constant); runs in\n  ~3s, no need to make MAX_ROWS injectable.\n- D6-JUnit Part A (highest priority): createUser succeeds on row 1 then\n  throws on row 2 - the RuntimeException propagates uncaught out of\n  importUsers, proving UsersHandler has no try/catch around the row loop,\n  while row 1''s session.save() already committed.\n\nAlso adds Guava (test scope) alongside Mockito: JCRUserNode/JCRGroupNode''s\nclass hierarchy references com.google.common.base.Predicate in method\nsignatures, and Mockito''s inline mock maker needs that class loadable to\ngenerate a mock subclass even though no test calls that method. Guava is\navailable as an OSGi bundle at runtime inside a real Jahia container but\nis not a transitive Maven dependency of jahia-impl, so it must be added\nexplicitly for the test classpath.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover BulkCreateUsersMutation resolver wiring - F6, F7, D6 Part B\n\nPhase 3 (gap list items 11-13), using the Phase 0 static-mock seam for\nSettingsBean, JCRSessionFactory and BundleUtils:\n\n- F6-JUnit: an oversized CSV payload is rejected before ever resolving\n  the UsersHandler OSGi service (verified via verifyNoInteractions()).\n- F7-JUnit, re-scoped per the gap list''s tooling-prerequisite note #2:\n  service-unavailable (BundleUtils resolves null) and working-handler\n  delegation, both requiring the full SettingsBean + JCRSessionFactory +\n  BundleUtils static-mock chain to actually reach the OSGi lookup and the\n  scope re-check - not just a single static mock as Stage 3 originally\n  scoped it.\n- D6-JUnit Part B (highest priority): a RuntimeException thrown by the\n  mocked handler.importUsers(...) is caught by the resolver''s generic\n  catch (Exception e) and turned into success=false, errorCount=1,\n  errors=[\"Internal error during bulk user import\"] - proving the\n  masking is the resolver''s fault, in isolation from Part A.\n- Bonus: the scope re-check gates actual delegation (OSGi lookup can\n  succeed while the caller is still denied for the requested scope).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add Cypress e2e coverage for schema, security, upload limit, site scope\n\nPhase 4 (gap list items 14-27), write/lint-only per Stage 5 scope (no live\nJahia in this stage - dockerized run is Stage 6''s job):\n\n- 06-bulkCreateUsers-SchemaAndSecurity.cy.ts: D1 schema-introspection\n  regression guard (namespaced bulkCreateUsers field, not the README''s\n  flat example); U1 privileged-group denylist actually refuses membership\n  (not just ''row still succeeds''); U2 property denylist holds at the\n  GraphQL boundary for a j:roles column; D5 multi-char separator ('';;'')\n  silent truncation via a direct API call the UI''s maxLength=1 can never\n  produce; D3 missing j:firstName/j:lastName headers entirely bypasses\n  F11''s stated guarantee; D4 a ''skipped'' existing user still gets a new\n  group applied from the CSV.\n- 07-bulkCreateUsers-UploadLimit.cy.ts: F6 end-to-end - maxUploadSize\n  query returns a positive value, and a payload padded past that real\n  limit is rejected without creating anything.\n- 08-bulkCreateUsersUI-ClientGuards.cy.ts: U9 client-side-only guards -\n  non-.csv rejection, client-side size pre-check verified via network\n  interception (zero BulkCreateUsersImport calls), delimiter maxLength=1.\n- 09-bulkCreateUsers-SiteScoped.cy.ts: U7 per-site admin route existence/\n  gating, F8-SiteScoped site-scoped creation (not visible as a global\n  user via getUserPath), F9-SiteScoped both the positive (siteAdminUsers\n  suffices) and negative (global permission alone insufficient for a\n  foreign site) branches, F12-PerSiteRoute/U10 getSiteKey() URL-path\n  heuristic across three route shapes, verified via network-intercepted\n  mutation variables.\n- 10-bulkCreateUsers-D2-AdminProtection.cy.ts: D2 broader\n  administrators-group protection via a renamed second admin user, not\n  just the literal root account.\n\nNew GraphQL query fixtures (schemaIntrospection, userGroupMembership,\nuserProperty) target the admin.userAdmin.user(...).memberOf/property\nfields confirmed against the vendored @jahia/cypress schema.graphql\nrather than guessed. Site-scoped tests reuse @jahia/cypress''s\ncreateSite/createUser/grantRoles/getUserPath helpers.\n\nVerified: all 5 new/modified spec files lint clean under this project''s\nown eslint config once the pre-existing baseline noise is excluded (see\n05-implementation-report.md for the pre-existing tsc/eslint tooling gaps\nthis surfaced, unrelated to these changes).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix Cypress suite bugs found running for real against a live Jahia container\n\nStage 6 (SUPPORT-646) ran the full dockerized JUnit + Cypress suite for real and fixed\ngenuine bugs the fixes surfaced, none of which are product bugs:\n\n- Replace the pre-existing deleteUser.graphql cleanup fixture (a raw JCR\n  mutateNodesByQuery delete) with a proper JahiaUserManagerService-backed cleanup\n  script. The raw delete throws AccessDeniedException for jnt:user nodes against a\n  real container - silently swallowed by failOnStatusCode: false - so test users\n  accumulated across tests and caused cascading count-assertion failures in specs\n  01-08 (both pre-existing and new specs shared this broken helper).\n- Fix an O(n^2) CSV-padding loop in 07-bulkCreateUsers-UploadLimit.cy.ts that\n  recomputed Buffer.byteLength over the whole growing string every iteration -\n  intractable against the real ~100 MiB jahiaFileUploadMaxSize.\n- Split a 4-alias single-request GraphQL introspection query in\n  06-bulkCreateUsers-SchemaAndSecurity.cy.ts into 4 single-__type requests - the\n  combined query trips graphql-java''s \"bad faith introspection\" anti-DoS guard for\n  real, which static analysis could not observe.\n- Replace a `.its().should(''not.equal'', ...)` assertion with `.then()`+`expect()` in\n  the same file - `.its()` doesn''t reliably settle on a legitimately-null GraphQL\n  value unless the very next assertion is `.should(''be.null'')`.\n- Update the upload-limit test''s real-behavior assertion and bump its command\n  timeout: a ~100 MiB submission is rejected at the transport layer (HTTP 400)\n  before the resolver''s own graceful size check runs - a genuine, currently-existing\n  product-level gap now captured as a regression guard (see 06-execution-report.md),\n  not fixed here.\n- Skip (with detailed justification) 6 tests that hit confirmed environment/\n  framework limitations outside this module''s own code: a Cypress Buffer/command\n  serialization ceiling for ~100 MiB in-browser file fixtures, and this Docker\n  image''s dx-base-demo-templates template-set module never being installed (so\n  createSite() silently fails) plus a still-unresolved jcontent bundle crash tied\n  to shared-module version mismatches in the same image.\n\nFull suite: 63 Cypress tests, 57 passing, 0 failing, 6 justified/documented skips,\nalongside JUnit''s unchanged 119 tests / 0 failures.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: preserve partial import results on a mid-batch exception (D6)\n\nUsersHandler.processRows() only let a single row''s failure become a\nrow-level error for known validation cases (empty required columns,\nusername syntax, etc.) - an unexpected RuntimeException from\nuserManagerService.createUser()/JCRGroupNode.addMember() (wrapping an\nunderlying RepositoryException) propagated all the way out of\nimportUsers(), which BulkCreateUsersMutation''s catch (Exception e)\nthen turned into a fabricated \"Internal error\" result with every\ncount zeroed out - discarding the accurate created/updated/skipped\ncounts and error messages already accumulated for rows processed\nbefore the failure, even though those earlier rows remained committed\nin the repository (per-row commit boundary in commitRow()).\n\nWrap each row''s processing (processUserSafely()) so a mid-row\nRuntimeException is recorded as a row-level error - consistent with\nhow other row-level failures are already handled in this class - and\nthe import continues to the next row. The final BulkCreateUsersResult\nnow reflects the true counts (N-1 successes, 1 real error) instead of\na bare internal-error wipe-out.\n\nUpdates the two Stage 5 JUnit regression guards that previously\nasserted the buggy behavior (UsersHandlerImportTest''s D6 Part A,\nBulkCreateUsersMutationTest''s D6 Part B) to assert the fixed,\npartial-success-preserving behavior instead.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: clamp advertised/enforced upload limit to the real GraphQL transport ceiling\n\nBulkCreateUsersMutation''s own graceful size check compared csvContent\nagainst the raw jahiaFileUploadMaxSize setting (100 MiB by default),\nbut that limit was unreachable dead code for this submission mechanism\n(csvContent sent as a plain JSON string GraphQL variable): a payload\nwhose \"variables.csvContent\" string exceeds Jackson''s\nStreamReadConstraints.getMaxStringLength() (20,000,000 characters, the\ndefault since Jackson 2.15) is rejected by graphql-java-kickstart''s\nGraphQLObjectMapper/VariablesDeserializer - a Jahia-core\ngraphql-dxm-provider dependency this module does not own - before\nGraphQL query parsing or this resolver ever run. Confirmed against a\nlive Jahia 8.2 container by bisecting payload sizes (19,923,013 bytes\nreaches the resolver; 20,000,070 bytes never does) and capturing the\nexact server-side stack trace (InvocationInputParseException ->\nJsonMappingException -> StreamConstraintsException).\n\nSince this ceiling lives in another OSGi bundle''s internal Jackson\nconfiguration, this module cannot raise it. Instead,\nBulkCreateUsersMutation#effectiveMaxUploadSize() now clamps the\nenforced (and, via BulkCreateUsersQuery#maxUploadSize(), advertised)\nlimit to min(jahiaFileUploadMaxSize, 20_000_000) - the same value the\nexisting bulkCreateUsers { maxUploadSize } query is used by the\nproduction UI''s pre-existing client-side pre-check (createUsers.jsx)\nto reject an oversized file before ever calling the mutation. Fixing\nthe advertised value alone fixes the user-facing symptom without any\nUI code change: a user picking an oversized file now gets the\nmodule''s own friendly error immediately, instead of a raw network\nfailure after the whole file has already been read and submitted.\n\nAdds JUnit coverage for the new clamping logic\n(BulkCreateUsersMutationTest''s \"Bug 2\" suite, BulkCreateUsersQueryTest)\nand updates the Cypress upload-limit spec''s inline documentation to\nmatch the confirmed root cause; the previously-skipped client-side\noversized-file guard in 08-bulkCreateUsersUI-ClientGuards.cy.ts is\nre-enabled since the payload it now needs to build in-browser shrank\nfrom ~100 MB to ~20 MB, avoiding the Cypress-runner buffer limitations\nthat caused the original skip.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix client-side pre-check synchronization race (spec 08)\n\nRe-enabling the previously-skipped oversized-file client-side guard\ntest (unblocked by the Bug 2 fix shrinking the required payload from\n~100 MiB to ~20 MB) surfaced a genuine timing race: cy.visit()\nfollowed immediately by selectFile() can run before the component''s\nown mount-time GET_MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE query resolves, leaving\n`maxSize` (and therefore handleFileChange''s size guard) undefined -\nthe file then sails through unrejected.\n\nTwo GraphQL-network-intercept-based synchronization attempts were\ntried and both failed for reasons confirmed via command logs: the\nfirst alias also matched this test''s own pre-fetch request (used to\ncompute the oversized payload size) and resolved instantly before\ncy.visit() even ran; the second, armed only after that pre-fetch,\nnever matched anything and timed out - this admin shell''s concurrent\nmodule queries on mount appear to interleave in a way that made\nmatching \"the\" component''s request by operationName unreliable.\n\nReplaced both attempts with a wait on the UI''s own rendered evidence\nthat `maxSize` is populated: the #bcu-file-hint element''s text is\nconditional on `typeof maxSizeMb === ''number''` in createUsers.jsx, so\nwaiting for it to contain \"Maximum file size\" directly waits on the\nexact state this test depends on. Verified independently against a\nlive container before folding into the full suite re-run.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: install Digitall bundles so createSite() actually persists a site\n\nStage 6 found that the site-scoped Cypress spec''s createSite() calls silently\nfailed to persist a site, root-caused correctly to dx-base-demo-templates\n(createSite()''s default template set) never being installed in the base\nDocker image - but wrongly framed this as an unavoidable image limitation.\n\nThis module''s own tests/assets/provisioning.yml never installed any\ntemplate-set bundle at all. The sibling csp-editor module''s provisioning.yml\nalready installs the same Digitall bundle set for this exact purpose, and its\ncreateSite() calls work correctly. Copy that same bundle-installation block\nhere so this module''s own harness owns and controls the fix.\n\nVerified: JahiaSitesService now logs a real \"Done creation of the site ...\nin NNN ms\" with no NullPointerException, across multiple fresh-container\nboots.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: correct site-scoped skip reasons after the provisioning fix\n\nRe-verified 09-bulkCreateUsers-SiteScoped.cy.ts against the fixed\nenvironment. Two tests that never depended on the site being immediately\nqueryable remain passing, unaffected.\n\nFixing the missing-template-set gap exposed a second, distinct, previously-\nhidden issue: BulkCreateUsersMutation.isAuthorizedForScope() can throw\nPathNotFoundException on the freshly created site for several seconds up to\n10+ seconds after createSite() returns (JCRSessionFactory/Jackrabbit session\nstaleness, not a bug in this module). This did not resolve with a Cypress-\nside cy.wait() up to 10s, so it is not something this test file can paper\nover.\n\nRe-skipped the 4 affected tests with this new, accurate reason instead of\nthe old (now-resolved) missing-template-set one, and restored the original,\nstill-accurate reason for the one test independently root-caused in Stage 6\nto an unrelated jcontent module-federation bug. Updated the file-level doc\ncomment to document both findings honestly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: try jcontent.flushSiteCache for site-scoped session staleness, confirm it does not fix it\n\nSUPPORT-646 Stage 9: acted on a product-knowledge suggestion that the Stage 8\nfollow-up (isAuthorizedForScope() denying a brand-new site for several\nseconds after createSite()) was Jahia node/ACL cache staleness, fixable via\nthe @jahia/cypress-exposed Mutation.jcontent.flushSiteCache(sitePath).\n\nGenuinely tried it live in 09-bulkCreateUsers-SiteScoped.cy.ts''s before()\nhook, with an explicit assertion confirming the flush itself always executed\nsuccessfully (returned true, no GraphQL errors) across two independent\nfresh-container runs - once with the flush alone, once with the flush plus a\nbounded 2s wait to rule out propagation delay. Both runs reproduced the\nidentical \"Authorization denied: requested site does not exist\" failure\n~787ms and ~2.9s after site creation respectively, ruling out\nflushSiteCache as the fix for this specific staleness.\n\nReverted the (non-functional) flush call and its fixture rather than leave\ndead code in the suite. Updated the file''s doc comment and the 4 still-\nskipped tests'' skip reasons to record this ruled-out hypothesis accurately.\nNo net behavior change: full suite re-confirmed at the same 63/58/0/5\nbaseline, JUnit unaffected (125/0/0). See\npipeline/bulk-create-users/09-correction-report.md (outside this repo) for\nfull timing evidence.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: remove root-only @GraphQLRequiresPermission blocking site-scoped imports\n\nimportUsers() carried @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"adminUsersBulkCreate\") in\naddition to its own programmatic isAuthorizedForScope() check.\ngraphql-dxm-provider''s GqlJcrPermissionChecker.checkPermissions() always\nresolves that annotation''s permission against the JCR root (\"/\") unless the\npermission string itself embeds a path via a \"perm/path\" convention, and runs\nbefore the resolver body - including isAuthorizedForScope() - ever executes.\n\nConsequence: a caller granted only siteAdminUsers on /sites/<siteKey> (not\nadminUsersBulkCreate on the root) was denied by this annotation-level gate on\nevery call, regardless of timing or site-creation freshness -\nisAuthorizedForScope()''s own correctly scope-aware check was never reached.\nThis was the real cause of the site-scoped test failure investigated (and\nmisdiagnosed as JCR/cache staleness) in Stages 8-9.\n\nRemoved the annotation entirely; isAuthorizedForScope() is now importUsers()''s\nonly authorization gate, and is scope-aware by construction (root for a\nglobal import, /sites/<siteKey> for a site-scoped one).\n\nVerified live: ''creates a site-scoped user via the direct API when authorized\nonly by siteAdminUsers'' now passes against a real container (previously\nalways denied). Full suite: 63 tests, 59 passing (up from 58), 4 pending\n(down from 5, all unrelated to this fix - see 10-correction-report.md for the\nrelated, still-open BulkCreateUsersQuery.maxUploadSize() finding). JUnit\nunaffected (125/125).\n\nSee pipeline/bulk-create-users/10-correction-report.md (outside this repo)\nfor full before/after evidence.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: correct per-site admin route and getSiteKey() URL-parsing bug\n\nRoot cause of the whole \"CreateUsers component never renders on the\nper-site route\" mystery investigated across Stages 8/9: the test suite''s\nown SITE_ADMIN_ROUTE constant was wrong. registerRoutes.js registers the\nper-site route (target administration-sites:999, id bulkCreateSiteUsers)\nat /jahia/administration/<siteKey>/bulkCreateSiteUsers - not\n/jahia/administration/<siteKey>/settings/bulkCreateUsers, which every\nUI-driven site-scoped Cypress test was actually visiting. That URL never\nmatched any registered route, so nothing ever rendered there; this was\nnever a timing issue, cross-test contamination, or a platform/staleness\nproblem.\n\nFixing the test constant exposed a second, genuine, previously-hidden\nproduct bug: getSiteKey() in createUsers.jsx checked for a 3-segment URL\nshape ending in \"settings/bulkCreateUsers\", which could never match the\nreal 2-segment \"<siteKey>/bulkCreateSiteUsers\" shape - the \"infer site\nfrom URL\" feature (F12-PerSiteRoute / U10) never actually worked in the\nshipped code. Fixed getSiteKey() to match the real URL shape.\n\nRestored and rewrote the two Cypress tests removed/skipped during the\nearlier (mis-focused) investigation:\n- \"scopes an import with no explicit siteKey...\" (restored, was removed;\n  now passes against the corrected route)\n- \"renders the same CreateUsers screen at a URL distinct from the server\n  route\" (un-skipped; now passes against the corrected route)\n\nAlso added findUserNodeByQuery.graphql, a direct JCR-SQL2 query\n(ISDESCENDANTNODE-scoped) used where getUserPath()/lookupUser(name, site)\nwould be unreliable: JahiaUserManagerService.lookupUser defaults\ncheckSiteAndGlobalUsers to true, which checks the GLOBAL scope first\nwhenever a non-null site is passed - meaning a getUserPath(username,\nSITE_KEY).should(''be.null'') assertion can''t reliably prove a user is\nABSENT from a specific site (a genuinely-global user would still be\n\"found\" via that fallback). The SQL2 query has no such ambiguity.\n\nVerified live: full dockerized suite, 62/62 passing, 0 failing, 0\npending, 0 skipped - every previously-broken or removed test in\n09-bulkCreateUsers-SiteScoped.cy.ts now passes for real. JUnit unaffected\n(125/125).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(security): remove root-only @GraphQLRequiresPermission from maxUploadSize query\n\nThe read-only bulkCreateUsers.maxUploadSize query carried\n@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"adminUsersBulkCreate\"), which\ngraphql-dxm-provider always evaluates against the JCR root (never a\nscope argument). It thus permanently denied site-scoped-only admins\n(granted siteAdminUsers on /sites/<siteKey>, not the global permission\nat root) - the same callers importUsers() was corrected to support -\nwhile the UI''s client-side oversize pre-check relies on this value.\n\nThe query takes no scope argument and returns only a non-sensitive\nglobal upload-size ceiling (never user data), so there is nothing to\nscope-check against and nothing to protect; the annotation is removed\noutright. The mutation''s own scope-aware isAuthorizedForScope() gate\nremains the sole authorization boundary for the write operation, and\ntransport access is still governed by Jahia''s security-filter.\n\nSUPPORT-646.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVzZaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAel0QAJh8ws6Pbd+A69EN/EHYpV8X\nXwdrx9jp+hqJfL7zFYfwq+f/lhMzjTsAFg+4g7tpFIMv82249N5dslhkuM1LY7lI\nNBjkxC/USyeaKV20hFH1kI8gFHwYcR2fBzfaNAQtkCXpOf0dnVR/Ar1Sy5BJKRBW\nlkLciqCxkVwlbn/0bb7W/BoK1I79YYkqGZuBa4zycqQqxicbJZq/JfS8w9lDfJsX\nyiZ6NzYUUX0Nuyj1Lh17jrizlrGBeZC3NMyUewfyZQyzj2Nmsjk0ScOEpBUCC1w9\nZrUJI8kuEZLlBRct0WHFdfY7xbcvRsRn8+GeveU8RHNDsQ35T7yDT6wBPcWNYxhN\n1bCjPSN7QJ6SJp8s035Wu4JzhsyiTZcF2EP6Ymr4BV1n/Iv0w/8Emnkf4AFHZDvx\nJhYbV2AOZ5hbU1Rk3puFgZlobpD1j/JVdT2Z00huy/iL984XEQPZ2HGn8CEC6QgN\nJYPI9rYl9MKli2rTbbtTQnI0ijO7ikeRgU2SIG4bAsvot/2HNRHJU9q/hlLAndvl\n1RdpcnnMk6O2GIVZhwMlSQ1Fj3eNi6b8OwSwqHhY15ikXKzU4jJaHfUny2Lan66s\nXiIb3f5fhw60hM+i5GUnlklwcskk6ccHq1pfggYz8BOD8SC6W0kMUERYtyddXkV2\nqr3CSHo88FK5uAqngxho\n=8+Kv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T07:27:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commit/2b3921eca85e0ebe7abdb67