ode_id":"C_kwDOIhiyTdoAKDdiYzE1NWRjMWRiOWM4NTExNTYyODI3YTM5Zjg5OWRlNDdlYWNjYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commit/1dc38ebebd1bcdcb89992f8edb0a5c52d4231933","sha":"1dc38ebebd1bcdcb89992f8edb0a5c52d4231933","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commits/1dc38ebebd1bcdcb89992f8edb0a5c52d4231933"}],"sha":"7bc155dc1db9c8511562827a39f899de47eaccbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commits/7bc155dc1db9c8511562827a39f899de47eaccbd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commits/1dc38ebebd1bcdcb89992f8edb0a5c52d4231933/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T06:59:39Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T06:59:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Quality, security & AAA accessibility hardening (blind-review cycle 1) (#10)\n\n* fix(backend): harden CSV import, persist groups on skip, force Java 17\n\n- Force Java 17 (maven-compiler-plugin <release>17</release>), matching the\n  Jahia 8.2 runtime and the sibling brute-force-login-protection module.\n- Security: make the property denylist case-insensitive so mixed-case\n  variants (J:roles, JCR:uuid, J:accountLocked) can no longer evade it;\n  add a regression test. Replace [A-Za-z0-9_] with \\w (Sonar S6353).\n- Bug: persist group memberships staged on the skipped-existing-user path\n  (commitRow no longer returns before save() for RESULT_SKIPPED).\n- Guard null csvContent (public OSGi service) and stop leaking the raw\n  IOException message to the client.\n- Extract GROUPS_COLUMN constant (Sonar S1192).\n- Hoist getErrors() out of the assertThatThrownBy lambda (Sonar S5778).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(ui): WCAG 2.2 AAA accessibility fixes and repair ESLint config\n\n- Rename .eslintrc -> .eslintrc.js so ESLint parses the JS config instead\n  of crashing on it as YAML; clear the errors this exposed (no-eq-null,\n  eqeqeq, jsx-sort-props).\n- Take the hidden file input out of the tab order (keyboard trap) and point\n  the visible label at the real input (bcu-csv-file-input).\n- Move focus to the visible message banner instead of invisible sr-only\n  live regions; restore focus to the file button after Cancel.\n- Replace disabled-checkbox required-column indicators with a non-interactive\n  status list (sr-only present/missing text; bcu-col-req-* ids preserved).\n- Enlarge the close button to a 44x44 target; raise hint/label contrast to\n  the AAA 7:1 threshold.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs+test: correct README authorization, reconcile column-selection spec\n\n- README Authorization section described adminUsers; the code uses the\n  fine-grained adminUsersBulkCreate gate with a scope-aware re-check. Rewritten.\n- Update 04-ColumnSelection Cypress spec for the required-column status-list\n  refactor (assert status items + presence glyph instead of checkbox state).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review follow-ups\n\n- Declare OSGi Require-Capability osgi.ee JavaSE 17 so a pre-17 JVM rejects\n  the bundle cleanly instead of failing with ClassFormatError.\n- Remove dead aria-describedby from the tabIndex=-1 hidden file input (the\n  hint is already associated with the focusable proxy button).\n- Assert j:password in the required-column ''all present'' Cypress test.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): close remaining WCAG 2.2 AAA gaps (cycle-2 review)\n\n- Required-column status list no longer wrapped in a <fieldset> (it holds no\n  form controls): use a labelled <div> + <ul aria-label> so AT does not\n  announce a misleading form group (SC 4.1.2).\n- Darken danger-red text #a4262c -> #8a1a1f so error banner, error list,\n  missing-required alert and missing badge all reach >=8:1 on their\n  backgrounds (SC 1.4.6 enhanced contrast, was ~6.4:1).\n- Raise the requirements-toggle focus-outline fallback to #006e9e (>=4.5:1)\n  (SC 2.4.13).\n- Give the file button and optional-column rows a 44px min target (SC 2.5.5).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"8957be5259e8c2b48e4d7f4b6a8a02ec170e17e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/trees/8957be5259e8c2b48e4d7f4b6a8a02ec170e17e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/commits/1dc38ebebd1bcdcb89992f8edb0a5c52d4231933","verification":{"payload":"tree 8957be5259e8c2b48e4d7f4b6a8a02ec170e17e9\nparent 208b17574fe462340f93446bbac2f926e8c72c53\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781852379 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781852379 +0200\n\nQuality, security & AAA accessibility hardening (blind-review cycle 1) (#10)\n\n* fix(backend): harden CSV import, persist groups on skip, force Java 17\n\n- Force Java 17 (maven-compiler-plugin <release>17</release>), matching the\n  Jahia 8.2 runtime and the sibling brute-force-login-protection module.\n- Security: make the property denylist case-insensitive so mixed-case\n  variants (J:roles, JCR:uuid, J:accountLocked) can no longer evade it;\n  add a regression test. Replace [A-Za-z0-9_] with \\w (Sonar S6353).\n- Bug: persist group memberships staged on the skipped-existing-user path\n  (commitRow no longer returns before save() for RESULT_SKIPPED).\n- Guard null csvContent (public OSGi service) and stop leaking the raw\n  IOException message to the client.\n- Extract GROUPS_COLUMN constant (Sonar S1192).\n- Hoist getErrors() out of the assertThatThrownBy lambda (Sonar S5778).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(ui): WCAG 2.2 AAA accessibility fixes and repair ESLint config\n\n- Rename .eslintrc -> .eslintrc.js so ESLint parses the JS config instead\n  of crashing on it as YAML; clear the errors this exposed (no-eq-null,\n  eqeqeq, jsx-sort-props).\n- Take the hidden file input out of the tab order (keyboard trap) and point\n  the visible label at the real input (bcu-csv-file-input).\n- Move focus to the visible message banner instead of invisible sr-only\n  live regions; restore focus to the file button after Cancel.\n- Replace disabled-checkbox required-column indicators with a non-interactive\n  status list (sr-only present/missing text; bcu-col-req-* ids preserved).\n- Enlarge the close button to a 44x44 target; raise hint/label contrast to\n  the AAA 7:1 threshold.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs+test: correct README authorization, reconcile column-selection spec\n\n- README Authorization section described adminUsers; the code uses the\n  fine-grained adminUsersBulkCreate gate with a scope-aware re-check. Rewritten.\n- Update 04-ColumnSelection Cypress spec for the required-column status-list\n  refactor (assert status items + presence glyph instead of checkbox state).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review follow-ups\n\n- Declare OSGi Require-Capability osgi.ee JavaSE 17 so a pre-17 JVM rejects\n  the bundle cleanly instead of failing with ClassFormatError.\n- Remove dead aria-describedby from the tabIndex=-1 hidden file input (the\n  hint is already associated with the focusable proxy button).\n- Assert j:password in the required-column ''all present'' Cypress test.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): close remaining WCAG 2.2 AAA gaps (cycle-2 review)\n\n- Required-column status list no longer wrapped in a <fieldset> (it holds no\n  form controls): use a labelled <div> + <ul aria-label> so AT does not\n  announce a misleading form group (SC 4.1.2).\n- Darken danger-red text #a4262c -> #8a1a1f so error banner, error list,\n  missing-required alert and missing badge all reach >=8:1 on their\n  backgrounds (SC 1.4.6 enhanced contrast, was ~6.4:1).\n- Raise the requirements-toggle focus-outline fallback to #006e9e (>=4.5:1)\n  (SC 2.4.13).\n- Give the file button and optional-column rows a 44px min target (SC 2.5.5).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNOjbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcA4QAAAMHcf3rfL4DKqGikiClcWs\nzVEZdnHSsLVVZ0X8fntdV5F6HOAuu7d9Uud5EqZ3ekJe9CId/zDTXGXUIHuXwn+i\nl4zoQJs0aYPpS58cI5vEdGW3gRCIKDS3md1KNkjmYX1lj+q1kQMX0hNTpBlkrD0l\nxCmi3doNLlaM88EvZQSQ5K7EtahUu/brc6VLnW+NI15f7aZbComjJ6pY6TFdSn8l\nYyNwAzh7Y45z+VcDOowEjw8wpQxKnGW2HnDMLnj/4nDOGzgxGLrtOH4OhE27awYG\n+ga3sEEB2EpkWdMgE0soQyd+UHyBOFavVPrCr+zUt9ElUr1Wg5c/JqAKIwjWnWZH\nJJ3xDie/94ZZ9cDG381bYMe804LrClH8ZlZ8EVd6FRKZoRZmiqMTm0oDocz3+YVP\nhE2c4pqVDZd6hsWV+AmWdarbVlJp9SYIfBebH2I1nwiuJ9Ep73Hn+cwlUQY+QQbw\nqnXWeaX/jK/2vLvjJjgEJQ/cxb/D9slXeo8PIh5uxfVmPNWds0tSFAcMyqchVyY3\nwB3CAPUT1anFsx0W9yXJFYF7oTisgxMMFbrpFlQLuJ8rLBoFeUWFYYAM3i/53Xqd\nSoyaI9mtxzm/BkCS9QJjrgACoFNKFD+TA4V9vDKd20gpHW60Q+GUJ8Fi/tdPPxqQ\nSik2PL7bw0kbfpYwXf7P\n=XrYd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-19T06:59:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commit/1dc38ebebd1bcdcb89992f8edb0a5c52d4231933","node_id":"C_kwDOIhiyTdoAKDFkYzM4ZWJlYmQxYmNkY2I4OTk5MmY4ZWRiMGE1YzUyZDQyMzE5MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commit/208b17574fe462340f93446bbac2f926e8c72c53","sha":"208b17574fe462340f93446bbac2f926e8c72c53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commits/208b17574fe462340f93446bbac2f926e8c72c53"}],"sha":"1dc38ebebd1bcdcb89992f8edb0a5c52d4231933","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commits/1dc38ebebd1bcdcb89992f8edb0a5c52d4231933"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/commits/208b17574fe462340f93446bbac2f926e8c72c53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:06:27Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:06:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#9)\n\n* feat: replace adminUsers with module-specific adminUsersBulkCreate permission\n\nDefine a module-scoped jnt:permission node (admin/adminUsersBulkCreate) in\npermissions.xml and update both @GraphQLRequiresPermission annotations in\nBulkCreateUsersMutationExtension and BulkCreateUsersQueryExtension to use\nthe new fine-grained permission instead of the global adminUsers permission.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: update requiredPermission to module-specific permission in frontend registration\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role\n\nAdd regression coverage for the fine-grained `adminUsersBulkCreate` permission\nacross the full stack, plus a server-scoped admin role that grants it without\nrequiring full server-administrator rights.\n\n- src/main/import/roles.xml: new `bulk-create-users-administrator` role\n  (j:roleGroup=server-role, j:nodeTypes=rep:root, j:privilegedAccess=true)\n  granting only `administrationAccess adminUsersBulkCreate`.\n- tests/cypress/e2e/05-bulkCreateUsers-Permissions.cy.ts: four tests proving\n  fine-grained granularity with a user granted ONLY the module role (never admin):\n    * GraphQL deny: user without the permission gets ''Permission denied''.\n    * GraphQL allow: user with the role succeeds on the read-only gated\n      `bulkCreateUsersMaxUploadSize` query.\n    * Admin UI hidden for the unprivileged user.\n    * Admin UI shown for the role-granted user.\n- tests/cypress/fixtures/graphql/query/maxUploadSize.graphql: fixture for the\n  read-only gated query used by the allow path.\n- pom.xml: bump module version 2.0.2-SNAPSHOT -> 2.0.3-SNAPSHOT (ships roles.xml).\n\nDouble-gating note: `bulkCreateUsersImport` additionally enforces an inner,\nhardcoded scope check requiring `adminUsers` (not `adminUsersBulkCreate`) on the\nJCR root, so a user holding only `adminUsersBulkCreate` is blocked there at the\ndata layer (domain message, not ''Permission denied''). The allow path therefore\ntargets the read-only `bulkCreateUsersMaxUploadSize` query, gated solely by the\nannotation, which the granted user passes fully.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: relax inner server-scope users permission to adminUsersBulkCreate so the fine-grained role can import end-to-end\n\nThe bulkCreateUsersImport mutation is gated by\n@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"adminUsersBulkCreate\") but its inner\nisAuthorizedForScope(null) check required the broader \"adminUsers\"\npermission on the JCR root (SERVER_USERS_PERMISSION). A user granted\nonly the fine-grained adminUsersBulkCreate role cleared the annotation\nbut was rejected at the data layer (\"Not authorized to manage users in\nthe requested scope\"), so the role could not actually import users.\n\nRetarget the server (global) scope check to adminUsersBulkCreate so it\nmatches the annotation; the role now works end-to-end. The per-SITE\nbranch is unchanged: it still accepts siteAdminUsers or the broad\nadminUsers (now via the new GLOBAL_USERS_ADMIN_PERMISSION constant) on\n/sites/<key>.\n\nUpdate the permission spec''s allow test to prove end-to-end usability:\nthe granted user (only adminUsersBulkCreate) drives the real\nbulkCreateUsersImport mutation with a one-user CSV and asserts success\n(createdCount=1, no errors). Imported user is cleaned up in after().\nThe deny test still asserts the annotation blocks an ungranted user\nwith ''Permission denied''.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"af30745a8d18b21491ef1f7140b28ac6f5263ab4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/trees/af30745a8d18b21491ef1f7140b28ac6f5263ab4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/commits/208b17574fe462340f93446bbac2f926e8c72c53","verification":{"payload":"tree af30745a8d18b21491ef1f7140b28ac6f5263ab4\nparent 852de39d3a6a6ab420e3573d29947ba94bf620dc\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781118387 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781118387 +0200\n\ntest: fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#9)\n\n* feat: replace adminUsers with module-specific adminUsersBulkCreate permission\n\nDefine a module-scoped jnt:permission node (admin/adminUsersBulkCreate) in\npermissions.xml and update both @GraphQLRequiresPermission annotations in\nBulkCreateUsersMutationExtension and BulkCreateUsersQueryExtension to use\nthe new fine-grained permission instead of the global adminUsers permission.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: update requiredPermission to module-specific permission in frontend registration\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role\n\nAdd regression coverage for the fine-grained `adminUsersBulkCreate` permission\nacross the full stack, plus a server-scoped admin role that grants it without\nrequiring full server-administrator rights.\n\n- src/main/import/roles.xml: new `bulk-create-users-administrator` role\n  (j:roleGroup=server-role, j:nodeTypes=rep:root, j:privilegedAccess=true)\n  granting only `administrationAccess adminUsersBulkCreate`.\n- tests/cypress/e2e/05-bulkCreateUsers-Permissions.cy.ts: four tests proving\n  fine-grained granularity with a user granted ONLY the module role (never admin):\n    * GraphQL deny: user without the permission gets ''Permission denied''.\n    * GraphQL allow: user with the role succeeds on the read-only gated\n      `bulkCreateUsersMaxUploadSize` query.\n    * Admin UI hidden for the unprivileged user.\n    * Admin UI shown for the role-granted user.\n- tests/cypress/fixtures/graphql/query/maxUploadSize.graphql: fixture for the\n  read-only gated query used by the allow path.\n- pom.xml: bump module version 2.0.2-SNAPSHOT -> 2.0.3-SNAPSHOT (ships roles.xml).\n\nDouble-gating note: `bulkCreateUsersImport` additionally enforces an inner,\nhardcoded scope check requiring `adminUsers` (not `adminUsersBulkCreate`) on the\nJCR root, so a user holding only `adminUsersBulkCreate` is blocked there at the\ndata layer (domain message, not ''Permission denied''). The allow path therefore\ntargets the read-only `bulkCreateUsersMaxUploadSize` query, gated solely by the\nannotation, which the granted user passes fully.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: relax inner server-scope users permission to adminUsersBulkCreate so the fine-grained role can import end-to-end\n\nThe bulkCreateUsersImport mutation is gated by\n@GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"adminUsersBulkCreate\") but its inner\nisAuthorizedForScope(null) check required the broader \"adminUsers\"\npermission on the JCR root (SERVER_USERS_PERMISSION). A user granted\nonly the fine-grained adminUsersBulkCreate role cleared the annotation\nbut was rejected at the data layer (\"Not authorized to manage users in\nthe requested scope\"), so the role could not actually import users.\n\nRetarget the server (global) scope check to adminUsersBulkCreate so it\nmatches the annotation; the role now works end-to-end. The per-SITE\nbranch is unchanged: it still accepts siteAdminUsers or the broad\nadminUsers (now via the new GLOBAL_USERS_ADMIN_PERMISSION constant) on\n/sites/<key>.\n\nUpdate the permission spec''s allow test to prove end-to-end usability:\nthe granted user (only adminUsersBulkCreate) drives the real\nbulkCreateUsersImport mutation with a one-user CSV and asserts success\n(createdCount=1, no errors). Imported user is cleaned up in after().\nThe deny test still asserts the annotation blocks an ungranted user\nwith ''Permission denied''.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbWzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA4UQAJDTJDvedrfmup/hi2TaR2sq\ntB26DQhhSu7jS0bHi6DhlVKitrinMh/MMFOJLXw94/zRJ+UOFAppTR8hfAzbFdov\n7nL7r4mSimu2eG/GSZZFAIwk53ab3G/BLOCRZSVnyFqa9piVgWGNwk4oiLiMX3bM\naw1pbMmM4yZcLRBaG7AIFiiktJYkLu09zoaoMfogcIEtKAubyOwNOIDOBz6RsFza\nIYnwnQplIz7xjz5O1a0C+YG7pi8MXnxMig7YsLTkmFhsqCTIK3YzMSvRpgnDwzz/\nKlu3HFsFKixXpGq3+m3/IoWEF8i81pQa2NNkdqyOarcnhn8uDm0EPnPTcprI7S5q\nPEjrRK7pEleccZ/mVbndFqrp960ETTnjhh8qBQUMaV1pwzDv8jET4u9DsUuut2NB\nyb85ZMPKGmrFVwRuzF5MT9ObI4rhfWAXvF1VyRUNp97Bg40471PMchFmO2U0NWIN\nHIKX/uIEGMgoriXR96fMQ5a0gSdUnQaRTZW/bDasPRujxVW646pe1kz01XzWRjUe\nc/10+krOrVx7v/qDQ4c+IGANA0MyicLSrWLFeVi94ZAX4ElstCVQEHuIKapT8oFc\nsI0D6AhU8UhN5xDkm094JCR4+VE9I/V2TJ1NOQJNkDrKxkxYVu14jcP45vFxHzo1\n9fQox6h9rfjUBk+7ERCb\n=6ixV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:06:28Z"}},"committer":{"avat