difiable wrapping of BulkCreateUsersResult\n  errors so the GraphQL result cannot be mutated post-construction.\n\nTests: +11 (separatorChar resolution x7, result immutability/null/counts x4).\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"c37766c47f0d1989c87379b039c89a31cddd8044","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/trees/c37766c47f0d1989c87379b039c89a31cddd8044"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/bulk-create-users/git/commits/4f8ea2f2fe91d1a6c1e98dffd93ac934f4458b66","verification":{"payload":"tree c37766c47f0d1989c87379b039c89a31cddd8044\nparent a7982c14ed43f148a87a2400e858ae7c56ea345b\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781071047 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781071047 +0200\n\nfix: harden handler input boundary and result immutability\n\nS1/R1: validate separator at the UsersHandler trust boundary\n  (separatorChar) so a null/empty separator no longer throws\n  StringIndexOutOfBoundsException when the OSGi service is called\n  directly (not via the GraphQL layer that defaults it).\nS2/R2: report and isolate rows with a blank/null username instead of\n  passing null into lookupUser/createUser.\nS3/R3: defensive copy + unmodifiable wrapping of BulkCreateUsersResult\n  errors so the GraphQL result cannot be mutated post-construction.\n\nTests: +11 (separatorChar resolution x7, result immutability/null/counts x4).\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoo/McACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lSFggAwsOcknA0ukMrxGRnpBnZVSvGGBphxBya6+1EJW4n0CQZnOId7HvmEH+Q\n/eoXKI7pXuXRd2fLG7toCpIYdlaEufyy3itTBHYXSvvLjj5sqcSEX54Lici+r0jj\njIUnNnNes+H76gqN+612NYZ813pPaz9l7+wLtscX0MQgFFXR6bOBZExFUlkcjLKc\nL3jaessPQJg/7kqhuLIF1I238xTeJLhAN3VcxFe5Tcwh/Sh/630B70cuP5tocIsr\nQLnFOtx/c8c6PCjXapLSCMj39XawUou+u81vp/fylrhhn+wK/K0ij0ADUzxxO1DP\nwVz6pGhw/cYC4rbnKVPkTnyy08NE4w==\n=Yw50\n-----EN